{"author":{"id":"038d65070aa747b6bc9d50939fa697ec871a40ed259db54429b255bbef2581d6"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1793002035,"nonce":"qVkzdc32oLawr5NZfGgSDiUXwlg=","title":"Keep unavailable definition targets from stopping the browser editor","message":"Go to Definition published a new active tab before reading its buffer. A definition response targeting an unmounted dependency or standard-library file then threw from MemoryWorkspace.getBytes during reactive editor rendering, stopping the browser application. Validate/load text before publishing the tab, and leave the current editor unchanged on a read failure. Report the filename in the toast and preserve the detailed path/error in the host log.\n\nThe real-browser regression reproduced the old failure for StringTools in the standard library. The new test covers opening a workspace Helper definition, attempting an unavailable library target, and continuing normal file navigation afterward. All pass in bin/web/browser-fixes; the verified bundle is staged in bin/web/rayde. This fixes crash containment; opening external library sources still requires an authorized read-only dependency mount.","files":null}]}